Checking the shunt, amplifier and sense-net geometry against the layout file; every view I'm citing is already open.

{"tables": {"Verdicts": [
{"Item": "SENSE-1", "Kind": "judgement", "Severity": "function", "Verdict": "fail", "Rests on": "net-_LOAD_RTN-r2c2.png (x 45.86 to 93.06, y 30.325 to 61.675); net-_AMP_FB-r2c2.png (same board place); net-_AMP_FB-r1c2.png and net-_AMP_OUT-r1c2.png (x 45.86 to 93.06, y -1.025 to 30.325); layer-F.Cu-r2c2.png (x 45.86 to 93.06, y 30.325 to 61.675); crop-U3.png (x 52.94 to 84.94, y 40.66 to 47.21)", "Why": "finding 1.1"},
{"Item": "SENSE-2", "Kind": "judgement", "Severity": "function", "Verdict": "not applicable", "Rests on": "placement-r1c2.png (U4, x 45.86 to 93.06, y -1.025 to 30.325); placement-r2c2.png (U3, x 45.86 to 93.06, y 30.325 to 61.675); facts.txt", "Why": "The schematic has no filter at a converter input and no reference capacitor. /AMP_OUT has exactly three pads: U3 pin 1 at (66.8625, 43.05), R2 pad 1 at (73.225, 46.375), and U4 pin 14 at (60.575, 14.5). U3 drives U4 directly, and R2 is the amplifier's feedback resistor, not a filter. The condition is not met."},
{"Item": "SENSE-3", "Kind": "judgement", "Severity": "function", "Verdict": "pass", "Rests on": "crop-U3.png (x 52.94 to 84.94, y 40.66 to 47.21); net-_AMP_FB-r2c2.png (x 45.86 to 93.06, y 30.325 to 61.675); placement-r2c2.png (same board place)", "Why": "The inverting input is U3 pin 4 at (69.1375, 44.95). Its net /AMP_FB has only R2 pad 2 at (71.575, 46.375) and R3 pad 1 at (71.575, 47.9) besides pin 4, so no track on it wanders. R2 is 2.82 mm from pin 4 in a straight line and 3.86 mm by track: 1.425 mm down, then 2.437 mm east. R3 pad 1 is 1.525 mm from R2 pad 2 and 1.86 mm by track. R2 centre (72.4, 46.375) is 3.56 mm from pin 4 and R3 centre (70.75, 47.9) is 3.7 mm from it. Both resistors sit at the pin. The route lengths differ from the plan row's figures (finding 1.4)."},
{"Item": "SENSE-4", "Kind": "judgement", "Severity": "function", "Verdict": "fail", "Rests on": "net-_AMP_OUT-r1c2.png (x 45.86 to 93.06, y -1.025 to 30.325); net-_AMP_OUT-r2c2.png (x 45.86 to 93.06, y 30.325 to 61.675); net-_AMP_FB-r1c2.png and net-_AMP_FB-r2c2.png (same board places); classes-r1c2.png and classes-r2c2.png (same board places); layer-B.Cu-r1c2.png and layer-B.Cu-r2c2.png; layer-F.Cu-r1c2.png and layer-F.Cu-r2c2.png; layer-In1.Cu-r1c2.png and layer-In1.Cu-r2c2.png; layer-In2.Cu-r1c2.png and layer-In2.Cu-r2c2.png", "Why": "finding 1.2"},
{"Item": "SENSE-5", "Kind": "judgement", "Severity": "function", "Verdict": "pass", "Rests on": "assembly-top-r2c2.png (x 45.86 to 93.06, y 30.325 to 61.675); assembly-top-r1c2.png (x 45.86 to 93.06, y -1.025 to 30.325); assembly-bottom-r2c2.png (same board place as the first); 3d-angled.png (whole board); placement-r2c2.png (same board place as the first)", "Why": "The heat sources are U2, the regulator at (44, 14), and U1, the phototriac at (31.81, 24) with its body running to about x 39.4. U3 is at (68, 44), so U2 is 38.4 mm from it and U1 is 41.2 mm from its origin; both are outside the analog sensing region (56, 28) to (92, 60). The nearest dissipating part is the shunt R1 at (60, 51), 10.6 mm from U3. R1 is the sensed element, with 0.05 ohm at 1.0 A (50 mW), so it is not a gradient source for the input parts. R2 at (72.4, 46.375) and R3 at (70.75, 47.9) sit together at pin 4, and no heat source is nearer either input's parts. The bottom side carries only test points."},
{"Item": "SENSE-6", "Kind": "rule", "Severity": "function", "Verdict": "fail", "Rests on": "check-report.txt (DESIGN PASS with no VIOLATION line; FIGURE SENSE-6 sensing clearance, board-rules.yaml sensing.clearance_mm, 0.5 mm; whole board); design-rules.md (no row for the rules sensing_clearance and sensing_override; whole board); classes-r2c2.png (x 45.86 to 93.06, y 30.325 to 61.675); classes-r1c2.png (x 45.86 to 93.06, y -1.025 to 30.325); net-_AMP_OUT-r2c2.png and net-_AMP_FB-r2c2.png (same board place as the first)", "Why": "finding 1.3"}
],
"Plan and free pass": [
{"Note": "SENSE-1 plan row: the sense track to U3 is not taken from R1's pad 1 as the row says (finding 1.1). The row's gain-resistor half is met: R3 returns to R1's ground pad 2 at its upper end through TP6 by its own track."},
{"Note": "SENSE-3 plan row: R2 is 3.86 mm by track from pin 4 against the row's 3.0 mm, and R3 is 1.86 mm from R2 pad 2 against the row's 1.5 mm (finding 1.4)."},
{"Note": "SENSE-4 plan row: AMP_OUT stays in the analog sensing region and crosses the +3V3 route to FB1 once at 45 degrees, as the row says. The row says nothing of LED_DRV, which runs beside AMP_OUT (finding 1.2)."},
{"Note": "SENSE-5 plan row is met: U3, R1, R2 and R3 are in the analog sensing region, and U2 and U1 are more than 20 mm away."},
{"Note": "The plan table has no row for SENSE-6, although the schematic carries a sensing front end. design-rules.md has no row for it either (finding 1.3). board-rules.yaml is not in the review folder, so the classes, figure and source it records could not be read."},
{"Note": "Free pass, sensing area only: LED_DRV on B.Cu runs (57, 13) to (57, 36) to (51, 36), inside the analog sensing region from y 28. FLOOR-2's row says LED_DRV stays outside it. This is recorded under finding 1.2 and belongs to the floorplan units."}
],
"Findings": [
{"Finding": 1, "Item": "SENSE-1", "Raised by": "SENSE-1", "Severity": "function", "What and where": "On net-_LOAD_RTN-r2c2.png, net-_AMP_FB-r2c2.png and layer-F.Cu-r2c2.png (x 45.86 to 93.06, y 30.325 to 61.675), the sense track to U3 pin 3 at (66.8625, 44.95) does not leave R1's pad 1 at (57.0375, 51), whose copper spans y 49.325 to 52.675. It runs (53.8, 55.5) to (53.8, 49.7) to (54.8, 48.7) to (57.0375, 48.7) to (58.0375, 47.7) to (61.8, 47.7) to (64.55, 44.95). It branches from the load track at (53.8, 55.5), beside J4 pin 2 at (52.8, 55.5), about 5.5 mm from the shunt pad. The 1.0 A load current therefore shares about 6.4 mm of 0.8 mm track with the sensed path before it reaches the shunt: (53.8, 55.5), the via (54.8, 55.5), (57.0375, 53.2625), pad 1. The sense track's end at (57.0375, 48.7), where the TP4 via sits, stands 0.225 mm short of the pad's top edge with no copper joining them, so the Kelvin connection is not at the shunt's pad.", "Rule": "no: a measurement could not state it from the board files, because which track is the sense branch and which carries load current is not in them, and a figure for it has no source outside the check. It needs judgement on the views.", "Added as": "", "Planning shortfall": "— The SENSE-1 plan row says the sense track to U3 leaves the same pad at its upper end, apart from the load track. Followed as written, that row meets the item, and the layout departs from it (the track branches at (53.8, 55.5)).", "Closed by": ""},
{"Finding": 2, "Item": "SENSE-4", "Raised by": "SENSE-4", "Severity": "function", "What and where": "On layer-B.Cu-r1c2.png, net-_AMP_OUT-r1c2.png, net-_AMP_OUT-r2c2.png and layer-B.Cu-r2c2.png, /AMP_OUT runs on B.Cu straight along x 58.75 from y 14.5 to y 34.9, then at 45 degrees to (65.3, 41.45). /LED_DRV, the controller's output that drives U1's LED, runs on B.Cu along x 57 from (57, 13) to (57, 36). It stays 1.75 mm centre to centre from the sense track, over about 20.4 mm (y 14.5 to 34.9) and inside the analog sensing region from y 28. This is a sensing track running alongside a drive track over a length, and LED_DRV is in Default, not a class SENSE-6 names. The plan's FLOOR-2 row has LED_DRV leaving along y 13 westward.", "Rule": "no: a measured rule for the parallel run length of a sensing net beside any other net could state it, but its only figure would have no source outside the check; no published document gives one, and SENSE-6's record figure holds only clearance between the classes the record names.", "Added as": "", "Planning shortfall": "shortfall: the SENSE-4 plan row names only the region, the distance from the crystal, U1 and the mains region, and the one crossing of the +3V3 route. It says nothing of drive or digital tracks such as LED_DRV running alongside AMP_OUT, so followed as written it would not have met the item.", "Closed by": ""},
{"Finding": 3, "Item": "SENSE-6", "Raised by": "SENSE-6", "Severity": "function", "What and where": "design-rules.md has no row for the rules sensing_clearance and sensing_override, and no row stating the figure 0.5 mm, the sensing and noisy classes the record names, or the key sensing.clearance_mm. The item's Passes requires the row, since the pre-order check holds the board only to the figure the record states and only the table shows it read against the item. The check's FIGURE line gives 0.5 mm from board-rules.yaml sensing.clearance_mm, but the record itself is not in the review folder and the layout-plan.md has no SENSE-6 row. The check reports no violation, and on classes-r2c2.png (x 45.86 to 93.06, y 30.325 to 61.675) the nearest sensing-to-Power gap is about 1.05 mm, where the AMP_OUT via at (65.3, 43.05) meets the LOAD_RTN track at y 44.95.", "Rule": "no: the presence of a row in design-rules.md is a property of a prose record, not of the board, so none of the five forms can state it. SENSE-6 already states the requirement and is judged on the table.", "Added as": "", "Planning shortfall": "shortfall: the plan has no SENSE-6 row at all, although the schematic carries a sensing front end, so followed as written it records no reason or figure for the item and its rules-table row was never planned.", "Closed by": ""},
{"Finding": 4, "Item": "PLAN-AND-FREE-PASS", "Raised by": "plan, SENSE-3 row", "Severity": "function", "What and where": "On crop-U3.png (x 52.94 to 84.94, y 40.66 to 47.21) and net-_AMP_FB-r2c2.png (x 45.86 to 93.06, y 30.325 to 61.675), the /AMP_FB tracks are longer than the SENSE-3 plan row states. R2's track from U3 pin 4 at (69.1375, 44.95) is (69.138, 44.95) to (69.138, 46.375) to (71.575, 46.375), which is 3.86 mm against the row's 3.0 mm. The track from R2 pad 2 to R3 pad 1 at (71.575, 47.9) is 1.86 mm through (71.975, 46.775) and (71.975, 47.5), against the row's 1.5 mm. The SENSE-3 item itself passes.", "Rule": "no: the plan row's figures are lengths of one board's tracks and no published source gives a figure, so it needs judgement against the plan.", "Added as": "", "Planning shortfall": "— The SENSE-3 plan row says R2 is just below and beside pin 4 by a 3.0 mm track and R3 is 1.5 mm further. Followed as written, the row meets the item, and the layout's tracks are longer than the row states.", "Closed by": ""}
]}}
